WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:02.878
he did not consult with

00:00:03.311 --> 00:00:04.446
Mcconnell about this decision to

00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:06.047
release this footage, Anderson.

00:00:06.181 --> 00:00:08.116
&gt;&gt; Manu Raju, appreciate it.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.385
I want to get perspective from

00:00:10.519 --> 00:00:12.254
"Washington post" contributing

00:00:12.387 --> 00:00:13.321
columnist George Conway.

00:00:13.321 --> 00:00:15.323
What do you make of this?

00:00:15.323 --> 00:00:16.424
Does it make sense what Mccarthy

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:16.892
is doing?

00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:17.359
&gt;&gt; No.

00:00:17.492 --> 00:00:20.896
It makes sense as a purely pr

00:00:21.329 --> 00:00:25.400
act to placify, to play indicate

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:26.968
tucker Carlson and to play

00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:28.737
indicate the Maga base.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:30.438
But it doesn't make any sense

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:31.873
from any other standpoint.

00:00:32.007 --> 00:00:34.943
For example, the idea that the

00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:35.944
defendants need this -- need

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:37.546
this in order to defend

00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:39.347
themselves.

00:00:39.347 --> 00:00:40.749
Well, the government already has

00:00:40.882 --> 00:00:41.349
this stuff.

00:00:41.349 --> 00:00:43.618
And if there is anything in

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:45.353
there exculpatory, they're

00:00:45.387 --> 00:00:46.655
required to produce it.

00:00:46.788 --> 00:00:47.622
And under Brady against

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:47.989
Maryland.

00:00:48.123 --> 00:00:49.391
And the fact of the matter is,

00:00:49.524 --> 00:00:51.359
what is it that it could

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:52.360
possibly show that would help

00:00:52.494 --> 00:00:53.028
these defendants?

00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:54.563
I mean, for example, if you

00:00:54.696 --> 00:00:56.097
catch one defendant smearing

00:00:56.231 --> 00:00:59.000
feces on the walls of the

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.403
capitol, and he later then uses

00:01:01.536 --> 00:01:03.371
the batter in another video and

00:01:03.371 --> 00:01:04.606
washes his hands, that doesn't

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:06.274
get you off of what he did in

00:01:06.408 --> 00:01:07.375
the first place.

00:01:07.375 --> 00:01:08.210
And showing that I don't know

00:01:08.343 --> 00:01:09.878
what else they could possibly

00:01:10.011 --> 00:01:12.414
glean from it, showing that

00:01:12.547 --> 00:01:13.615
capitol police officers at some

00:01:13.748 --> 00:01:15.884
points allowed people to come

00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:16.451
in?

00:01:16.585 --> 00:01:18.453
Well, they did that in part

00:01:18.587 --> 00:01:20.488
because they were trying to

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:21.857
prevent a bloodbath.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.626
So I just don't understand what

00:01:24.759 --> 00:01:27.529
it is that they're trying to

00:01:27.662 --> 00:01:30.498
accomplish other than to just

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:31.967
perpetuate the January 6th lie,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.068
that there was nothing

00:01:33.401 --> 00:01:34.970
extraordinary that happened on

00:01:35.403 --> 00:01:35.470
January 6th.

00:01:35.604 --> 00:01:36.838
&gt;&gt; From a legal perspective, how

00:01:36.972 --> 00:01:38.240
much trouble do you think fox

00:01:38.373 --> 00:01:41.409
News is in with this dominion

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:41.610
lawsuit?

00:01:41.743 --> 00:01:44.079
&gt;&gt; It's incredible.

00:01:45.547 --> 00:01:48.884
I litigated libel cases, one in

00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:51.086
particular in my practice 25

00:01:51.419 --> 00:01:51.686
years ago.

00:01:52.153 --> 00:01:53.755
I litigated lots of other cases.

00:01:53.889 --> 00:01:56.725
When you a libel case and you're

00:01:56.858 --> 00:01:57.759
the plaintiff's lawyer, you

00:01:57.893 --> 00:01:59.794
don't expect to get anything

00:01:59.928 --> 00:02:00.395
remotely like this.

00:02:00.528 --> 00:02:02.430
This is sort of like a -- these

00:02:02.564 --> 00:02:03.965
cases are like a kaleidoscope.

00:02:04.099 --> 00:02:05.433
What you have is sometimes you

00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:06.434
turn it one way and the

00:02:06.568 --> 00:02:07.836
reporters look a little careless

00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:09.437
and they look like they're

00:02:09.504 --> 00:02:09.905
ignoring something.

00:02:10.038 --> 00:02:11.539
The other way, you can see how

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:12.874
they might have believed this

00:02:13.008 --> 00:02:14.276
story to be true.

00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:15.977
And what's really remarkable is

00:02:16.111 --> 00:02:17.445
that this comes in the context

00:02:17.545 --> 00:02:20.949
of the most different.

00:02:21.082 --> 00:02:23.451
Standard, the most standard that

00:02:23.451 --> 00:02:25.020
you could possibly apply in a

00:02:25.453 --> 00:02:26.454
libel case, which is "The new

00:02:26.588 --> 00:02:27.622
York Times" against Sullivan

00:02:27.756 --> 00:02:31.826
standard, which governs the

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.662
libel claims on matters of

00:02:33.795 --> 00:02:34.663
public concern against public

00:02:34.796 --> 00:02:34.996
figures.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.532
And that requires -- it's a bit

00:02:37.666 --> 00:02:38.733
of a misnomer.

00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:40.502
People talk about it being the

00:02:40.635 --> 00:02:41.870
standard of actual malice.

00:02:42.003 --> 00:02:44.072
The supreme court uses that

00:02:44.205 --> 00:02:44.372
word.

00:02:44.506 --> 00:02:45.006
But malice isn't required.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.310
You heard the term "Reckless

00:02:48.443 --> 00:02:48.743
disregard."

00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:49.511
Reckless isn't enough.

00:02:49.644 --> 00:02:51.012
It's not enough the reporter

00:02:51.146 --> 00:02:52.213
blew past some facts.

00:02:52.347 --> 00:02:55.016
What you have to show, in a case

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:58.119
from 1968 called St. Amon versus

00:02:58.253 --> 00:02:59.054
Thompson that says what you have

00:02:59.487 --> 00:03:01.489
to show to show reckless

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:04.359
disregard is at a minimum, the

00:03:04.492 --> 00:03:05.160
publisher of the information or

00:03:05.493 --> 00:03:07.696
the broadcaster of the

00:03:07.829 --> 00:03:09.164
information actually entertained

00:03:09.497 --> 00:03:11.066
serious doubts as to the truth

00:03:11.499 --> 00:03:12.867
of what was being reported.

00:03:13.001 --> 00:03:15.503
And here it's you have that in

00:03:15.503 --> 00:03:16.271
droves, at multiple levels.

00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:17.505
I don't have you the fact

00:03:17.505 --> 00:03:19.975
checker, you have the anchors,

00:03:20.108 --> 00:03:21.509
you have Rupert Murdoch, all

00:03:21.609 --> 00:03:22.911
agreeing that this was false.

00:03:23.044 --> 00:03:25.513
And you never see in a libel

00:03:25.513 --> 00:03:26.281
case, you just virtually never

00:03:26.414 --> 00:03:28.850
see in a libel case the libel

00:03:28.984 --> 00:03:30.251
plaintiff moving for summary

00:03:30.385 --> 00:03:31.019
judgment, which is a judgment

00:03:31.152 --> 00:03:32.287
without a trial, saying there is

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.655
really no issue to go to the

00:03:33.788 --> 00:03:33.955
jury.

00:03:34.089 --> 00:03:35.790
It's all one-sided.

00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:37.192
Because the standard against

00:03:37.525 --> 00:03:38.393
libel plaintiffs is so high.

00:03:38.526 --> 00:03:40.929
And here they made that motion.

00:03:41.062 --> 00:03:41.796
And it's not a bad motion.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.865
I think ultimately it will be

00:03:43.999 --> 00:03:45.767
heard before a jury, but if the

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.037
judge actually granted certainly

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.705
on falsity, but they're not

00:03:50.839 --> 00:03:53.541
disputing falsity, if the judge

00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:55.543
even granted on actual malice

00:03:55.677 --> 00:04:00.548
and the state of mind, "The new

00:04:00.682 --> 00:04:01.850
York Times" standard, that

00:04:01.983 --> 00:04:03.218
wouldn't be crazy, and that's

00:04:03.551 --> 00:04:03.618
remarkable.

00:04:03.752 --> 00:04:06.554
&gt;&gt; Do you think it affects -- if

00:04:06.688 --> 00:04:08.890
the ruling, if it does go to

00:04:09.024 --> 00:04:10.525
trial, and there is a big fine

00:04:10.658 --> 00:04:12.327
for fox, does that impact, do

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.429
you think kind of right wing

00:04:14.562 --> 00:04:15.864
media how it behaves going to

00:04:15.997 --> 00:04:19.567
the 2024 election, or even the

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:19.768
former president?

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:22.037
Fox is in this weird position

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.571
now of how -- if the former

00:04:23.571 --> 00:04:25.206
president guess on their air and

00:04:25.573 --> 00:04:27.575
repeats lies about dominion

00:04:27.709 --> 00:04:29.778
voting machines and the last

00:04:29.911 --> 00:04:30.912
election, what did they do?

00:04:31.046 --> 00:04:33.748
&gt;&gt; Well, it's hard to say,

00:04:33.882 --> 00:04:35.717
because the law isn't any

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.152
different after a judgment is

00:04:37.585 --> 00:04:39.587
entered against fox than it was

00:04:39.721 --> 00:04:39.921
before.

00:04:40.055 --> 00:04:41.589
You're not supposed to lie.

00:04:41.723 --> 00:04:42.991
You can't tell lies.

00:04:43.124 --> 00:04:44.793
You're going to be held liable

00:04:44.926 --> 00:04:45.593
for lies.

00:04:45.593 --> 00:04:46.828
And yet foxes that been taking

00:04:46.961 --> 00:04:47.595
this crazy view.

00:04:47.595 --> 00:04:49.731
And you saw it in the excerpts

00:04:49.864 --> 00:04:51.132
of Rupert Murdoch's deposition.

00:04:51.266 --> 00:04:52.700
You see it in some of the

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.536
statements that their pr flakes

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:57.605
have been producing which is oh,

00:04:57.639 --> 00:04:58.807
well, fox didn't endorse the big

00:04:58.940 --> 00:04:59.074
lie.

00:04:59.207 --> 00:05:00.708
Maybe some of our anchors did.

00:05:00.842 --> 00:05:01.943
It doesn't work that way.

00:05:02.077 --> 00:05:02.977
You know, that Anderson.

00:05:03.111 --> 00:05:04.746
If you say something and you

00:05:04.879 --> 00:05:06.414
report something and you

00:05:06.548 --> 00:05:10.685
describe it as fact or even as

00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:12.987
something short of established

00:05:13.121 --> 00:05:15.623
fact, CNN is on the hook if you

00:05:15.723 --> 00:05:16.424
libel somebody.

00:05:16.558 --> 00:05:18.793
And your state of mind matters.

00:05:18.927 --> 00:05:19.627
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:05:19.627 --> 00:05:24.599
&gt;&gt; It's crazy what -- they're

00:05:24.732 --> 00:05:25.633
taking a position like these

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:26.868
people, we pay them.

